MagicPods Cinnamon is an unofficial, AI-assisted Cinnamon frontend.
It is not an official MagicPods or Apple product.

The Bluetooth backend is MagicPodsCore, developed by Aleksandr Maslov
and Andrei Litvintsev. The frontend integration references the upstream
MagicPodsLinux project by Aleksandr Maslov. Original notices are
retained in their source files.

MagicPodsCore source: https://github.com/steam3d/MagicPodsCore
Pinned revision: 04af4bdeb5cbdc7cb6eeba9b0acf2076cc6d3c16
MagicPodsLinux reference: https://github.com/steam3d/MagicPodsLinux

MagicPods Cinnamon release modification, 2026-11-24: Core
`src/main.cpp` binds the WebSocket to IPv4 loopback. Core uses the
pinned upstream notification timing. See LICENSE for GPL-3.0 terms.

The matching magicpods-cinnamon-source.tar.gz contains the patched Core,
complete bundled dependency sources, notices, and build/install scripts.
Distribute it with the runtime archive from the same download location.

Third-party code in the Core executable or its headers:
  sdbus-c++ v1.6.0 — LGPL-2.1 with its upstream linking exception.
  uSockets v0.8.7 — Apache-2.0.
  uWebSockets v20.58.0 — Apache-2.0.
  nlohmann/json v3.11.3 — MIT.
  toml++ v3.4.0 — MIT.

The upstream license texts are in licenses/ in the runtime archive and
in the vendor trees in Corresponding Source. The runtime archive does
not include third-party shared system libraries. These are supplied by
the destination distribution.
